<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victor Amadeus I, Duke of Savoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1587">1587</a>–<a href="/years/1637">1637</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victor Amadeus I was Duke of Savoy from 1630 to 1637, son of Charles Emmanuel I. Married to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christine-of-france">Christine of France</a>, a daughter of Henry IV, he made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> at Cherasco in 1631, gaining part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> while secretly yielding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinerolo">Pinerolo</a>, and later fought alongside the French against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. His death in 1637, followed by that of his eldest son, opened a disputed regency and a civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-i-duke-of-savoy.jpg" alt="Victor Amadeus I, Duke of Savoy" width="296" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanna Garzoni · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vittorio_Amedeo_I_of_Savoy1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
